 "nl": [
  "No packet from database may enter backup, even for services open to everyone.",
  "Any zone may connect to database over DNS over UDP 53 and HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "Any zone may connect to ops over DNS over UDP 53 and NTP (UDP 123).",
  "ops may use any UDP port towards backup, except SNMP (UDP 161), which must be blocked.",
  "Allow backup to connect to research using NTP (UDP 123) and RTSP (TCP 554).",
  "Allow database to connect to hr using syslog (UDP 514) and LDAP (TCP 389).",
  "Allow research to connect to hr using LDAP (TCP 389) and MySQL (TCP 3306) and SMTP (TCP 25).",
  "Permit any TCP port from ops to database but deny SMB (TCP 445), RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Block TFTP (UDP 69), SNMP (UDP 161) from ops to iot-sensors; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "Hosts in ops may reach iot-sensors over NTP (UDP 123) and SMTP (TCP 25).",
  "database must accept RTSP (TCP 554) and RDP (TCP 3389) and IMAP (TCP 143) from backup.",
  "backup must accept LDAP (TCP 389) from iot-sensors.",
  "research must accept SSH (TCP 22) and NTP (UDP 123) and LDAP (TCP 389) from hr.",
  "Hosts in research may reach hr over SMB (TCP 445) and HTTPS (TCP 443) and MySQL (TCP 3306).",
  "Permit any TCP port from iot-sensors to ops but deny Telnet (TCP 23), SMB (TCP 445), RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Any zone may connect to hr over HTTPS (TCP 443) and NTP (UDP 123).",
  "backup must accept PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and LDAP (TCP 389) and HTTPS (TCP 443) from ops.",
  "research is isolated: it may only reach backup on DNS over UDP 53, and nothing else.",
  "iot-sensors offers NTP (UDP 123) to every zone.",
  "Permit any UDP port from research to backup but deny TFTP (UDP 69), SNMP (UDP 161).",
  "backup must accept NTP (UDP 123) and SMTP (TCP 25) and SSH (TCP 22) from ops.",
  "Block PostgreSQL (TCP 5432), RDP (TCP 3389) from iot-sensors to hr; the rest of TCP ports 1024-65535 between them is allowed.",
  "Hosts in iot-sensors may reach ops over MySQL (TCP 3306) and SMB (TCP 445).",
  "ops must accept NTP (UDP 123) and RTSP (TCP 554) and PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) from hr.",
  "Hosts in ops may reach backup over syslog (UDP 514) and SNMP (UDP 161) and HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "Deny all traffic from database to hr (this overrides any public service).",
  "hr offers NTP (UDP 123) and HTTP (TCP 80) to every zone.",
  "Any zone may connect to database over DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Allow database to connect to research using PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "Permit TCP ports 1024-65535 from backup to hr but deny MySQL (TCP 3306), PostgreSQL (TCP 5432), RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Make HTTPS (TCP 443) and HTTP (TCP 80) on database reachable from all internal zones."
 ],
